(vector (map (:adr/consequences "{:shared_pipeline \"chart/graph/math/document generation in any kotoba actor can go through a shared, portable, dependency-free EDN pipeline (d3 scale/shape -> svg path strings; katex parse -> MathML; tex AST -> LaTeX source; force3d simulation -> node positions) instead of ad hoc JS interop or bespoke per-project code\", :composability \"kotoba-lang/d3's path-string output and kotoba-lang/katex's MathML output are wire-compatible with kotoba-lang/svg/html's Hiccup-like [:tag {attrs} children] shape without a hard dependency on those repos\", :independent_from_rust_kami_graph \"force3d gives kotoba a JVM/cljs/SCI/GraalVM-portable force-directed layout not requiring the Rust kami-engine toolchain, at the cost of a separate implementation from kami-graph (accepted: different runtime targets and consumers)\", :v1_scope_narrow \"Barnes-Hut/octree optimization (force3d), full TeX math grammar / glyph-level layout (katex), curved-line interpolation and axis rendering (d3), and a TeX engine/compiler (tex) are all explicitly deferred, not blocking this registration\", :deferred_unrelated_wip \"the primary working directory's kami-provider-catalog manifest/repos.edn WIP remains uncommitted and unaffected by this ADR's registration, landed independently via a separate clean worktree\"}"), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "kotoba-lang/tex is an EDN-first LaTeX-source *document generator* (Hiccup-like AST -> string), not a TeX engine/compiler" "kotoba-lang/katex is a native TeX-math-subset parser + EDN AST + MathML renderer, not a JS/npm KaTeX.js interop wrapper and not a full glyph-level font-metric layout engine" "kotoba-lang/force3d is a pure-functional, portable 3D force-directed simulation on plain EDN node/link maps, independent of (not a WASM bridge to) the Rust kami-graph crate in orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine" "kotoba-lang/d3 covers the d3-scale + d3-shape analogue only (scales, line/area/arc generators, pie-layout) -- no DOM selection/data-binding, no transitions, no force layout (that is force3d)" "all four repos are plain nouns with no -clj suffix, zero third-party runtime deps, .cljc, registered under kotoba-lang org via manifest/repos.edn :extra-projects")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "kotoba-lang-viz-typesetting-substrate"), (:adr/related (vector "CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2607011130-kotoba-svg-did-edn-substrate.edn" "manifest/repos.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine/CLAUDE.md")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607012000-kotoba-lang-viz-typesetting-substrate"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-01"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607012000: `kotoba-lang/{tex,katex,force3d,d3}` — visualization/typesetting EDN-first substrate\n\nStatus: Accepted\nDate: 2026-07-01\n\n## Context\n\nAn owner survey asked whether `d3`, `force3d`, `katex`, `tex` were already lib-designed\nas `.cljc`/kotoba substrate under `kotoba-lang`. They were not: the only adjacent\nprior art was `orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine/kami-graph`, a **Rust** crate providing\nforce-directed graph layout inside the WGPU game engine, and `main.tex` files that\nare LaTeX paper *sources* (build artifacts), not a library. No math-rendering or\nchart/scale/shape library existed at all.\n\nThe owner decided to build native, from-scratch implementations (not JS/npm\ninterop wrappers) of all four, following the same EDN-first pattern already\nestablished by `kotoba-lang/svg`, `kotoba-lang/html`, `kotoba-lang/css`, and the\nfoundational stdlib libs (`coll`, `json`, `spec`, ...): plain nouns (no `-clj`\nsuffix), zero third-party runtime deps, single-or-few well-tested `.cljc`\nnamespaces, registered as new `kotoba-lang` repos via `manifest/repos.edn`\n`:extra-projects`.\n\n## Decision\n\nFour new repos, each scaffolded and pushed independently (parallel subagents,\none repo each, no shared-file conflicts), then registered together in one\nmanifest commit:\n\n| Repo | Scope (v1) | Explicitly out of scope (v1) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `kotoba-lang/tex` | EDN→LaTeX-source *document generator* (Hiccup-like `[:command {opts} & args]` / `[:env \"name\" {opts} & body]`, `render`, `escape`, `document`/`section`/`itemize`/`enumerate`/`frac`/`sqrt`/`math`/`tabular` helpers) | A TeX engine/compiler (no pdflatex invocation, no page layout, no font metrics) |\n| `kotoba-lang/katex` | Recursive-descent parser from a TeX-math-like string to a pure EDN math AST (`\\frac`, `^`/`_`, `\\sqrt`/`\\sqrt[n]{}`, Greek letters, common operators/relations, `{}` grouping), plus an AST→MathML EDN/XML renderer | Full glyph-level font-metric layout (what KaTeX.js actually does); matrices, `\\left`/`\\right` auto-sizing, accents, text mode |\n| `kotoba-lang/force3d` | Pure-functional 3D force-directed graph simulation on EDN data (`{:nodes [...] :links [...]}`, composable forces `charge`/`link`/`center`/`collision`, `simulation`/`tick`/`simulate` integrator with alpha cooling) — the portable analogue of `d3-force-3d`, independent of the Rust `kami-graph` crate | Barnes-Hut/octree optimization (documented as a future improvement, brute-force O(n²) charge force is v1) |\n| `kotoba-lang/d3` | `kotoba.lang.d3.scale` (linear/log/ordinal/point/band scales) and `kotoba.lang.d3.shape` (line/area/arc path generators, pie-layout angle computation) — the `d3-scale`+`d3-shape` analogue, output wire-compatible with `kotoba-lang/svg`'s `[:path {:d ...}]` shape | DOM selections/data-binding (`d3-selection`), transitions/animation, force layout (that's `force3d`) |\n\nAll four: zero third-party runtime deps, real test suites (all green — see\nVerification below), private GitHub repos under the `kotoba-lang` org, plain\nnouns per the org naming convention (no `-clj` suffix).\n\n## Verification\n\n| Repo | HEAD SHA | Tests |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `kotoba-lang/tex` | `3491a3a74234b706761d00dfbbdda74e4c447816` | 19 tests / 45 assertions, 0 failures |\n| `kotoba-lang/katex` | `63ce122a66c0b7b0379c48d0ba086bfd4b1c561a` | 20 tests / 53 assertions, 0 failures |\n| `kotoba-lang/force3d` | `f1a76c2e227230b2a384c15a06d8990d5ff65ed9` | 10 tests / 17 assertions, 0 failures (one real charge-force sign-convention bug found and fixed during scaffolding) |\n| `kotoba-lang/d3` | `eed5dd8cc1b5cd8009c3559e776872564c976d30` | 17 tests / 52 assertions, 0 failures |\n\nManifest registration: `manifest/repos.edn` `:extra-projects` gained the four\npaths (`orgs/kotoba-lang/{tex,katex,force3d,d3}`), `manifest/west.yml` was\nregenerated with `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs` in a clean worktree checked\nout from `origin/main` tip (avoiding the local superproject checkout's\nunrelated in-progress `kami-provider-catalog` WIP on `repos.edn`), with the\nfour new repos' working trees copied in so `working-head` could resolve their\npins directly. A before/after name→revision diff confirmed the regeneration\ntouched **only** the four new entries — no other project's pin moved or was\nremoved (the large raw line-diff was pure alphabetical-resort churn from\ninserting four entries into a sorted list, not data drift). `--check` passes.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Chart/graph/math/document generation in any kotoba actor can now go through\n  a shared, portable, dependency-free EDN pipeline instead of ad hoc JS\n  interop or bespoke per-project code.\n- `kotoba-lang/d3`'s path-string output and `kotoba-lang/katex`'s MathML output\n  are designed to compose with `kotoba-lang/svg`/`kotoba-lang/html` (Hiccup-like\n  shapes) without a hard dependency on them.\n- `force3d` gives kotoba a JVM/cljs/SCI/GraalVM-portable force-directed layout\n  that does not require the Rust `kami-engine` toolchain, at the cost of not\n  sharing an implementation with `kami-graph` (acceptable: different runtime\n  targets, different consumers).\n- v1 scope is intentionally narrow (see tables above) — broadening (Barnes-Hut,\n  full TeX math grammar, curved-line interpolation, axis rendering) is future\n  work, not blocking initial registration.\n- The pre-existing uncommitted `kami-provider-catalog` WIP on the primary\n  working directory's `manifest/repos.edn` was left untouched (preserved via\n  stash/restore, never discarded) — this ADR's registration was landed via an\n  independent clean worktree specifically to avoid bundling unrelated WIP into\n  this commit.\n\n## Alternatives\n\n- **JS/npm interop wrappers around real d3.js/KaTeX.js**: rejected by the\n  owner in favor of native implementations, consistent with the org's\n  EDN-first, zero-third-party-runtime-dep convention for all sibling\n  substrate libs (`svg`, `html`, `css`, `did`, ...).\n- **Bridging to the existing Rust `kami-graph` crate via WASM for `force3d`**:\n  rejected — adds a WASM bridge dependency and couples a portable JVM/cljs\n  library to the game-engine build toolchain for no clear benefit over a\n  straightforward native reimplementation of the (well-known, small) algorithm.\n- **Full feature-parity reimplementations (complete TeX math engine, full\n  d3.js module set, LaTeX compiler)**: rejected as v1 scope — these are each\n  independently large undertakings; a focused, well-tested core surface\n  (documented explicitly per-repo) ships faster and matches how other\n  `kotoba-lang` substrate libs (`coll`, `svg`) were scoped."), (:adr/decision "{:new_repos [{:path \"orgs/kotoba-lang/tex\", :remote \"kotoba-lang\", :visibility :private, :head_sha \"3491a3a74234b706761d00dfbbdda74e4c447816\", :scope \"EDN Hiccup-like LaTeX document generator: render/escape/raw/command/env primitives; document/section/subsection/subsubsection/itemize/enumerate/item/math/display-math/frac/sqrt/tabular helpers\", :tests \"19 tests / 45 assertions, 0 failures (clojure -M:test)\"} {:path \"orgs/kotoba-lang/katex\", :remote \"kotoba-lang\", :visibility :private, :head_sha \"63ce122a66c0b7b0379c48d0ba086bfd4b1c561a\", :scope \"kotoba.lang.katex.parse: recursive-descent TeX-math-string -> EDN AST (frac, sup/sub/supsub, sqrt/nth-root, greek letters, common operators/relations, grouping, :unknown fallback). kotoba.lang.katex.mathml: AST -> MathML EDN -> XML string\", :tests \"20 tests / 53 assertions, 0 failures (clojure -M:test)\"} {:path \"orgs/kotoba-lang/force3d\", :remote \"kotoba-lang\", :visibility :private, :head_sha \"f1a76c2e227230b2a384c15a06d8990d5ff65ed9\", :scope \"kotoba.lang.force3d.core: simulation state {:nodes :links :forces :alpha ...}; composable forces charge/link/center/collision (all x/y/z, true 3D); simulation/tick/simulate integrator with alpha decay\", :tests \"10 tests / 17 assertions, 0 failures (clojure -M:test); one real charge-force sign-convention bug found and fixed during scaffolding (negative :strength was attractive instead of repulsive)\"} {:path \"orgs/kotoba-lang/d3\", :remote \"kotoba-lang\", :visibility :private, :head_sha \"eed5dd8cc1b5cd8009c3559e776872564c976d30\", :scope \"kotoba.lang.d3.scale: linear-scale/linear-invert, log-scale/log-invert, ordinal-scale, point-scale, band-scale. kotoba.lang.d3.shape: line-generator, area-generator, arc-generator (large-arc-flag + full-circle edge cases handled), pie-layout\", :tests \"17 tests / 52 assertions, 0 failures (clojure -M:test)\"}], :scaffold_method \"four independent general-purpose subagents, one repo each, run in parallel (no shared-file writes -- each confined to its own new repo directory and git history; manifest/repos.edn, manifest/west.yml, and ADR authorship were explicitly withheld from all four and centralized afterward)\", :manifest_registration {:repos_edn \"added the four orgs/kotoba-lang/{tex,katex,force3d,d3} paths to :extra-projects\", :west_yml \"regenerated via nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs inside a fresh git worktree (/tmp/wt-viz-libs) created from origin/main tip (git worktree add -b manifest/register-viz-libs), with the four new repos' working-tree checkouts copied into the worktree's orgs/kotoba-lang/ so working-head could resolve their pins; all other ~450 existing projects' working trees were absent from this worktree by design, so gen-west-manifest.cljs fell back to their existing west.yml-recorded revisions unchanged\", :verify \"a name->revision diff of west.yml before/after regeneration showed added=[d3 force3d katex tex], removed=[], changed-revisions=[] -- confirming the regeneration touched only the four new entries; nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check passed (exit 0); pin == child-repo HEAD confirmed for all four (matches the head_sha values above)\", :why_clean_worktree_not_primary_checkout \"the primary superproject working directory had unrelated uncommitted WIP on manifest/repos.edn (kami-provider-catalog split) and a local branch that could not git merge --ff-only origin/main (persistent shallow-graft 'unrelated histories' error despite gh api compare confirming a true fast-forward); a clean worktree off origin/main tip avoided both bundling that WIP and fighting the shallow-merge issue\", :preserved_wip \"the pre-existing manifest/repos.edn WIP in the primary working directory (/Users/junkawasaki/github/com-junkawasaki) was never discarded -- verified via git stash push/pop round-trip, left in place, untouched, for its own owner to land separately\"}}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/problem "{:source \"owner request 2026-07-01: asked whether d3/force3d/katex/tex were already cljc/kotoba lib-designed under kotoba-lang; answer was no (only orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine/kami-graph, a Rust force-directed-layout crate, and .tex paper-source build artifacts existed); owner then said 'ok, do it' and, via clarifying questions, chose: all four libs, native implementation (not JS/npm wrappers), registered as new kotoba-lang repos\", :investigated [\"grep across orgs/kotoba-lang for d3/force3d/katex/tex found no dedicated library -- kami-graph (Rust, inside kami-engine) and main.tex paper sources (LaTeX build artifacts, not a library) were the only hits\" \"kotoba-lang naming convention confirmed via directory listing: svg, did, html, css, rdf, turtle, shacl, ooxml, drawingml, coll, json, spec, wit, async, device -- all plain nouns, no -clj suffix\" \"kotoba-lang/coll (deps.edn/README/src/test shape) and kotoba-lang/svg (Hiccup-like EDN element convention, [:tag {attrs} & children] -> deterministic string render) used as the canonical templates for all four new repos\" \"GitHub name availability confirmed via gh api repos/kotoba-lang/{d3,force3d,katex,tex} (all 404 before creation) and org write access confirmed via gh api orgs/kotoba-lang\"], :risk \"the primary superproject working directory had a large pre-existing uncommitted WIP on manifest/repos.edn (kami-provider-catalog split, ~90 line diff) at session start; a naive local edit + nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs + commit in that same working tree would have bundled or clobbered that unrelated WIP. Separately, the local branch (codex/ec-maturity-20) was on an old shallow-grafted commit and could not git merge --ff-only origin/main even after git fetch --deepen=30 (persistent 'refusing to merge unrelated histories' from a stale shallow graft boundary), despite gh api compare confirming a pure fast-forward (ahead_by 28, behind_by 0, merge_base == local tip)\"}"), (:adr/alternatives "[{:option \"JS/npm interop wrappers around real d3.js/KaTeX.js\", :rejected_because \"owner explicitly chose native implementation over interop wrapping, consistent with the zero-third-party-runtime-dep, EDN-first convention already established by svg/html/css/did and the rest of the kotoba-lang substrate family\"} {:option \"bridge force3d to the existing Rust kami-graph crate via a WASM boundary\", :rejected_because \"adds a WASM bridge dependency and couples a portable JVM/cljs library to the game-engine build toolchain; the force-directed-layout algorithm itself is small and well-known enough that a straightforward native reimplementation was simpler and kept the library dependency-free\"} {:option \"attempt full feature parity (complete TeX math engine incl. glyph/font-metric layout, full d3.js module set incl. selections/transitions, a real LaTeX compiler)\", :rejected_because \"each is independently a multi-month undertaking; scoped v1 surfaces (documented per-repo above) ship a solid, well-tested core now, matching how kotoba-lang/coll and kotoba-lang/svg were themselves scoped as focused rather than exhaustive\"} {:option \"regenerate manifest/west.yml directly in the primary superproject working directory\", :rejected_because \"that working directory had unrelated uncommitted WIP on the same file (kami-provider-catalog split) and a local branch stuck behind origin/main by a shallow-graft artifact that git merge --ff-only could not resolve even after git fetch --deepen=30; a clean worktree off origin/main tip avoided bundling the unrelated WIP and avoided fighting the shallow-merge issue entirely\"}]"), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607012000: kotoba-lang/{tex,katex,force3d,d3} — visualization/typesetting EDN-first substrate"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))